# The dispatcher's vet entrypoint: the wire shape of a call, one
# schema per tool, GENERATED from the registry's argument schemas so
# the two can never drift. A call {tool, arguments} is vetted at
# $.guard.<tool>.
#
# This lives OUTSIDE registry.aon, unmarked, because a type() mark on
# any ancestor of the vet anchor silently drops required-key
# enforcement: a call missing a required argument vets "valid", and
# copy() does not win the force back (README, gap 7). Packing here
# from the marked $.argschemas keeps enforcement AND keeps
# registry.aon cleanly generable.
@"registry.aon"

guard: pack($.argschemas, close({
  tool: key()
  arguments: _
}))
